From: Surface Overdrive <noreply@surface-overdrive>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu3: requeue a dropped startup frame with the 0.7.2 CIO2 interface

libcamera 0.7.2 dropped the request argument of CIO2Device::queueBuffer(): the buffer alone goes back to the CIO2. Patch
0016 (drop startup frames) is written against 0.7.1, where the request is passed too; this adapts its one call.

---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
index 2c5d4f3..884ac00 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
@@ -1747,7 +1747,7 @@ void IPU3CameraData::cio2BufferReady(FrameBuffer *buffer)
 	 */
 	if (startupFramesToDrop_ > 0) {
 		startupFramesToDrop_--;
-		cio2_.queueBuffer(request, buffer);
+		cio2_.queueBuffer(buffer);
 		return;
 	}
 
